// Elimination (Load/Store) -- SOURCE program.
//
// rmm-zoo property: elim_ls (Elimination / sound).
// Source: Moiseenko, Podkopaev & Koznov, "A Survey of Programming Language
//         Memory Models" (2021), Tables 1-2 -- the Elimination group;
//         Sevcik's thesis, fig. 1.4 (redundant write-after-read elimination).
//
// The store x := r1 writes back the value just read from x, so it is redundant
// in isolation; opt.lit drops it. This is the one Elimination cell the zoo
// mostly records as UNSOUND (elim_ls is false for 15 of the 23 models that have
// the cell, RC11 and C11 among them) -- the write is observable to other threads
// even though it changes nothing locally. The multi-threaded witness for that
// unsoundness is litmus-tests/sevcik_thesis/Skip/Redundant Write after Read
// Elimination.lit; this pair is the local transformation it refutes.
x := 0;
y := 0;
r1 := x;
x := r1;
r2 := x;
if (r1 = r2) {
  y := 1
} else {skip}
